WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.795 --> 00:00:06.025
Can a robot learn from its own imagination,
without new expert demonstrations?

2
00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:12.250
Consider placing two ducks
into their matching bowls.

3
00:00:16.195 --> 00:00:21.400
The earlier policy fails to place the
pink duck and does not complete the task.

4
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:30.375
Instead of collecting more demonstrations,
we generate candidate experience.

5
00:00:31.345 --> 00:00:35.475
One scene, multiple imagined
video-action trajectories.

6
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.950
Each chunk predicts future frames,
actions, and a robot state.

7
00:00:42.395 --> 00:00:46.245
The next chunk uses generated
history and the predicted state,

8
00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:48.725
with the initial frame as an anchor.

9
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.800
No candidate actions are executed
externally during generation.

10
00:00:55.395 --> 00:01:00.350
The vision-language model checks goal
completion and object consistency.

11
00:01:01.195 --> 00:01:04.675
The blue duck misses its
bowl, so the placement fails.

12
00:01:06.395 --> 00:01:09.595
A second duck appears
while the original remains.

13
00:01:09.595 --> 00:01:12.350
Visual voting rejects this candidate.

14
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.800
An inverse dynamics model reconstructs
actions from the generated video.

15
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:25.175
Here, candidate three looks promising, but
its action mismatch exceeds the threshold.

16
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:31.800
After action verification, visual
votes confirm the endpoints.

17
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.675
Only candidate four is retained.

18
00:01:35.645 --> 00:01:39.445
Verified prefixes are pooled
across tasks and rounds,

19
00:01:39.445 --> 00:01:43.175
then mixed with original data
to train a shared policy.

20
00:01:46.245 --> 00:01:51.050
Now, the updated policy places both
ducks into their matching bowls.

21
00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:58.775
This is a new physical execution,
not the imagined rollout.

22
00:02:04.595 --> 00:02:07.295
The key is not just imagining success,

23
00:02:07.295 --> 00:02:11.225
but turning verified imagination
into training experience.
